{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdMAxqdJb844R1GDqHXDt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the code, I see that publish_planner_jobs is called from turn.rb, but the planner information (which worker produced what) is not readily available at this point. \n\nHowever, if I look at the run_planner_turn method more carefully, I can see there's no prior_worker context here. The planner decision is being handled by the PlannerDecisionSubmission service.\n\nLet me look back at the PlannerDecisionSubmission to see where the SpawnRequest is being created. Looking at the persist_decision! method (line 150-165 of planner_decision_submission.rb), it calls Turn.run_planner_turn which then calls Planner.publish_planner_jobs.\n\nSo the flow is:\n1. PlannerDecisionSubmission.call receives the planner's decision\n2. It calls Turn.run_planner_turn with next_step and following_steps\n3. Turn.run_planner_turn calls Planner.publish_planner_jobs to create the SpawnRequest\n\nThe challenge is: how do I know what the prior worker produced? The prior worker is the one that caused the planner to be called. Let me look at when a planner_turn is triggered.\n\nLooking at Turn.run_worker_turn (lines 8-91), when a worker completes, it creates a planner request. So the prior worker would be the one whose SpawnRequest was just fulfilled.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the architecture:\n1. A worker completes and calls worker_turn\n2. This creates a new planner SpawnRequest\n3. The planner runs and calls PlannerDecisionSubmission\n4. The planner creates a new SpawnRequest for the next worker\n5. The next worker should inherit artifacts from the prior worker\n\nSo the \"prior worker\" from the planner's perspective is the one who created the planner request. I need to:\n1. Find the most recent worker before the planner request was created\n2. Get that worker's produced_artifacts\n3. Populate inherited_artifacts based on some logic (e.g., all of them, or selective)\n\nLet me look at how I can access the prior worker from within the publish_planner_jobs method or from the planner_turn context. The task description mentions that \"planner decision methods examine prior_worker.produced_artifacts\", which means I need to pass the prior worker context into the planner methods so they can access and evaluate what artifacts should be inherited by the next worker.\n\nThe publish_planner_jobs method seems like the right place to handle this—I should enhance it to accept prior worker information, determine which artifacts to inherit based on planner logic, and populate the inherited_artifacts field in SpawnRequest along with reasoning for the inheritance decisions. I need to check if the run or decision object already contains prior worker or request information that I can leverage.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":248,"cache_read_input_tokens":53777,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":248},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b4af749-2a39-4012-a7f2-ddf24e6c5426","uuid":"84b4031b-cc6c-4a4d-8291-6f0d30ef3bae","timestamp":"2026-07-24T16:09:12.216Z","request_id":"req_011CdMAxmqMKXwjtEPVRNg5A"}
