{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdMAyntdQgBPCCSYNZyBL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the code, in persist_decision! (line 163-173 of planner_decision_submission.rb), we have access to:\n- decision (the PlannerDecision object)\n- decision.run (the Run)\n- params (the decision parameters)\n\nFrom decision, I can access:\n- decision.spawn_request (the request that triggered the planner)\n\nThe spawn_request that triggered the planner is the one created by the prior worker's turn. So I should look at the fulfillment history to find the prior worker.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. The PlannerDecision is triggered by a SpawnRequest with requested_role: \"planner\". This request is created by a worker (via Turn.run_worker_turn). \n\nThe key insight is: I need to find the prior worker who created this planner request. Looking at the Turn.run_worker_turn code (lines 56-79), the planner_request is created with:\n- asked_by: \"worker\"\n- scope: PLANNER_FOLLOWUP_SCOPE (\"workflow-plan.md\")\n- context: includes \"Worker #{nickname} (role #{role})...\"\n\nSo I can find the prior worker by looking at workers in the run and finding the most recent one whose status is not \"running\" (i.e., has stopped and reported).\n\nOr more directly, I can look at the most recent SpawnRequest before the current planner request that was fulfilled by a worker.\n\nLet me think about the architecture more carefully:\n1. Worker A completes and calls worker_turn\n2. worker_turn creates a new SpawnRequest for planner (asked_by: \"worker\")\n3. The planner runs and calls PlannerDecisionSubmission\n4. PlannerDecisionSubmission should look at Worker A's produced_artifacts\n5. PlannerDecisionSubmission should pass this to Turn.run_planner_turn\n6. Turn.run_planner_turn should pass this to Planner.publish_planner_jobs\n7. Planner.publish_planner_jobs should populate inherited_artifacts in the new SpawnRequest\n\nThe implementation needs to thread prior_worker_artifacts through the call chain. I'll need to add a method to extract the prior worker's artifacts, modify Turn.run_planner_turn to accept and forward them, and update Planner.publish_planner_jobs to set inherited_artifacts on newly created spawn requests.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":452,"cache_read_input_tokens":55016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":452},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b4af749-2a39-4012-a7f2-ddf24e6c5426","uuid":"0f67f50c-69fa-4eed-b41e-a655394df41b","timestamp":"2026-07-24T16:09:23.091Z","request_id":"req_011CdMAynCD1fUrKjRxC5Dxp"}
